  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the advent of the spring season, Prometeo prepared to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He was instructed in Sageness by Ishtar.  Prometeo 
practiced well and improved his ability in Sageness.  He discovered nothing 
in his sagely experiments.
  During early summer, Prometeo was instructed in Sageness by Ishtar.  
Prometeo practiced for months and his skill in Sageness increased.
  All characters of this high level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Prometeo invented nothing worthy of note in his sagely researches.
  With the advent of the late summer season Prometeo was instructed in the 
art of Sageness by Ishtar.  Prometeo tried to improve his Sageness, but the 
task seemed beyond his aptitude.  His experience raised his aptitude in 
Sageness.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.

  A fleet of mighty ships carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Sea province of Mare 
Imbrium, held by Prometeo.  Mare Imbrium was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb's fleet.  Uga-Buga Makumb leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 2 
Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  During fall, Prometeo was instructed in the art of Sageness by Ishtar.  
Prometeo practiced diligently for many weeks and his skill in Sageness 
increased.
  Your characters of this exalted level are awarded the following Advanced 
Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Prometeo discovered nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early winter season Prometeo tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task was beyond his ability.  He invented nothing in his 
sagely experiments.

  Prometeo was visited by a hero from Valhalla, named Two-Headed Eagl!  The 
characteristics for this great King from Game 27 are given in your 
"CHARACTERS" report.
  If Two-Headed_Eagl searches a feature, any monetary treasure 
Two-Headed_Eagl captures will be given to you.  If Two-Headed_Eagl captures 
a magic treasure, Two-Headed_Eagl will give it to your King when he departs 
for Valhalla, or you can order Two-Headed_Eagl to Give it to one of your 
characters.  You can do anything you want with the magic item 
Two-Headed_Eagl came with, but the item will leave at the end of his stay 
with you.  Except for the rules given in this paragraph, Two-Headed_Eagl can 
generally be treated just like your other Heroes, and can be affected by any 
spell except Resurrection.  The main limitation in using Two-Headed_Eagl is 
that Two-Headed_Eagl has only enough patience to practice with you for one 
of the phase(s) Two-Headed_Eagl is with you.  Two-Headed_Eagl will leave at 
the end of the last phase Two-Headed_Eagl is scheduled to serve you, after 
all battles have been fought.  Two-Headed_Eagl can lead armies, but when 
Two-Headed_Eagl returns to Valhalla, the armies will normally be left 
leaderless in the province they are in.  If Two-Headed_Eagl has the armies 
in a province you don't own, they will be transferred to your 
lowest-numbered leader in the same province, or at last resort, the garrison 
commander in an adjacent province owned by you.  If no leader is available, 
the armies will be disbanded.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Prometeo for this year.


  Prometeo treated with his ally Bradipo I (#2).  Prometeo treated with his 
ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Prometeo treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).
Prometeo treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Prometeo treated with his ally 
Giovanna (#7).  Prometeo treated with his ally Circe (#8).  Prometeo treated 
with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Prometeo's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 1 gold in revenue.  8 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Prometeo was left 
with 42 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Marlon
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to sweet spring, and I prepared to carry out my 
urgent orders.  I journeyed to Tesawa.  While adventuring, I encountered no 
wandering monster.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I moved into Orielle.  In my 
travels, I saw no monsters.
  In late summer, I rode into Macondo.  I encountered no monster.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  I was tutored in 
the art of Sageness by Ishtar.  I practiced well and improved my ability in 
Sageness.  I invented nothing in my sagely researches.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I was instructed in Sageness 
by Prometeo.  I tried to practice my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
natural ability.  I invented nothing in my sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


From: Tonto, Squire to Ishtar
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to sweet spring.  Ishtar tried to improve his Sageness, 
but the task seemed beyond his natural ability.  In his sagely researches, 
he discovered a fabulous invention called the Trap Finding Dust!  The 
following benefits are conferred by the Trap Finding Dust:
  Trap Finding Dust is a specially ground and colored dust which, when 
thrown onto a stone surface, helps to identify joints in the stone which may 
be traps or secret compartments.  Its effect is to raise the Thief ability 
of all of the characters of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Ishtar tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his ability.  He discovered nothing 
valuable in his sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer came.  Ishtar rehearsed and 
practiced his Sageness and improved noticeably.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached level 6 in Sageness.  Your 
characters of this exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  SAGE'S UNIVERSITY:  The Sage gains an additional plus 1 level when 
researching inventions if he is at his University (the location is shown in 
the Characters listing).  All percentage bonuses are cumulative.
  Ishtar discovered nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the fall season Ishtar tried to improve his Sageness, 
but the task was beyond his ability.  He invented nothing worthy of note in 
his sagely experiments.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Ishtar invented nothing 
valuable in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Tonto, Squire to Ishtar


From: Berthier, Squire to Girard
To: Prometeo

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Girard set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He travelled to Belladonna.  Girard saw no monsters.
  In early summer, Girard journeyed to Marzuq.  Girard observed the area 
while we were on the march and now 100% of Marzuq has been explored.  While 
adventuring, Girard saw no marauding monster.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer arrived.  Girard moved into Orielle.
In his travels, he saw no wandering monster.
  With the coming of the fall season, Girard rode into Macondo.  While 
adventuring, Girard saw no monster.
  In early winter, Girard was tutored in the art of Sageness by Prometeo.  
Girard tried to practice his Sageness, but the task was beyond his natural 
aptitude.  He discovered nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Berthier, Squire to Girard


